# netsurf: Vita hardware-test diagnostics, round 3 (frontends/vita)
# Generated 2026-09-23
#
# After hardware run 2 (doc 10): the fetch-stall hypothesis behind round 2's
# automatic fetch_pump() was wrong -- run 2's engine log shows the fetch
# finishing and HTML creation failing (vitaSDK's newlib has an empty iconv;
# fixed by building libparserutils WITHOUT_ICONV_FILTER). So:
# - the automatic fetch pump is removed; the per-page "no document yet" and
#   load-status lines stay;
# - log.txt: run 2 left it untouched while netsurf.log was written. It is
#   now one handle opened at boot, line-buffered, every write checked, a
#   failure reported with its errno in netsurf.log, and every line mirrored
#   there as "DIAG ...". The autotest marker reports fopen/fclose errors.

